---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
const site = Astro.site?.toString().replace(/\/$/, '') || '';
---
<Base title="For agents: MCP and REST · Process Cookbook" description="Search and fetch recipes from an AI agent: a public MCP endpoint and a REST mirror, no sign-in." >
  <section class="section wrap" style="padding-bottom: 80px; max-width: 820px;">
    <h2 style="font-size: 30px; margin-bottom: 12px;">For agents</h2>
    <p class="muted" style="font-size: 17px; margin-bottom: 28px;">The same index that powers search here is open to any agent, with no sign-in.</p>
    <div class="article" style="max-width: none;">
      <h2 style="font-size: 22px;">MCP</h2>
      <p>Streamable HTTP at <code>{site}/mcp</code>. Tools: <code>find_recipes</code> (query, optional domain, for, limit; without a query it lists the shelf), <code>get_recipe</code> (id, optional part: human, model or all; build from all, since the model is an appendix to the human part) and <code>list_domains</code> (every domain with its recipes: id, title, summary). Queries can be in the person's own words and in any language: search matches by meaning as well as by words. A search answers with <code>fits</code>: false means nothing on the shelf is close, and the hits are only the nearest. Add it to Claude as a custom connector, or to any MCP client by URL.</p>
      <h2 style="font-size: 22px;">REST</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><code>GET /api/search?q=volunteer+cats&amp;domain=nonprofit&amp;limit=5</code>: ranked matches as JSON; without <code>q</code>, the recipes of a domain or of everyone; <code>&amp;debug=1</code> adds the words searched and the closest recipes by meaning with their similarity.</li>
        <li><code>GET /api/recipes/tnr-program?part=human|model|all</code>: one recipe as JSON, with its Markdown and the file's header verbatim. <code>model</code> is Details for building alone; the rules, promises and setup questions it depends on are in <code>human</code>.</li>
        <li><code>GET /r/tnr-program.md</code>: the recipe file itself.</li>
        <li><code>GET /api/domains</code>: domains with counts and their recipes.</li>
        <li><code>GET /llms.txt</code>: the whole library as a list an agent can read in one go.</li>
      </ul>
      <h2 style="font-size: 22px;">Rules</h2>
      <p>Everything is CC BY 4.0: build it anywhere, credit the cookbook. Be reasonable with request rates. A recipe's canonical source is its file in the <a href="https://github.com/Fibery-inc/process-cookbook">GitHub repo</a>; this site and the endpoint are printed from it on every push.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
